{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"\"My commits landed on master/main\" - the recovery for a repo that autocommitted onto its default branch before the 'branches always' rule: move those commits onto a new branch and put the local default back where origin has it, without touching the working tree. fetch --prune -> checkout -b <branch> at the default's current HEAD -> branch -f <default> origin/<default> (a pointer move, never a checkout) -> push -u origin <branch>. Nothing is rewritten and nothing force-pushed: the commits keep their history under the new name; run update_from_master afterwards to fold in what origin gained meanwhile (behind_base says how much). Requires origin, being ON the default branch, and at least one commit origin/<default> lacks (otherwise: start_branch). Refuses an existing branch name, conflicts, a merge in flight. Uncommitted edits ride along untouched (carried). Returns {status, msg, branch, default, base, carried_commits, behind_base, published, publish_err, carried, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"branch","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ljkngp1a0740a1c47j1","readers":[],"time":1788653264434,"username":"system","writers":[]}